From: Ivo Nunes <ivo@nunes.uk>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 21:24:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Audio: set_bus_layout() announces the new layout

AudioServer emits bus_layout_changed when a bus is added, removed or
moved, but not when set_bus_layout() replaces them all, so anything
that follows the buses (Purr's Options, which keeps the player's
volume for each) never hears of a layout a game loads at run time.
The new layout keeps its own volumes then, whatever the player chose.

set_bus_layout() now emits bus_layout_changed once the new buses are
in place.

No upstream issue yet.

Test: after AudioServer.set_bus_layout() at run time, the player's
saved bus volume is in effect again (Purr's samples/options).
---
 godot/servers/audio/audio_server.cpp | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/godot/servers/audio/audio_server.cpp b/godot/servers/audio/audio_server.cpp
index d5f542b0..e642ca12 100644
--- a/godot/servers/audio/audio_server.cpp
+++ b/godot/servers/audio/audio_server.cpp
@@ -1648,6 +1648,9 @@ void AudioServer::set_bus_layout(const Ref<AudioBusLayout> &p_bus_layout) {
 	unlock();
 
 	// Samples bus sync.
+
+	// Like adding, removing or moving a bus, a whole new layout is announced.
+	emit_signal(SNAME("bus_layout_changed"));
 }
 
 Ref<AudioBusLayout> AudioServer::generate_bus_layout() const {
